P7. Claim 5c: rational 3-cycle x^2-29/16 at x0=-7/4
==============================================================================
(i) orbit: ['-7/4', '5/4', '-1/4', '-7/4']
    FINITE-EXACT: {-7/4, -1/4, 5/4} is an exact 3-cycle and an arithmetic progression with difference 3/2.
    What is PROVED in the repo (cite, do not re-prove): 01-canon/theorems/THM-4139-*: the complete rational
      preperiodic graph of x^2-29/16 is eight quarter-integers plus this one 3-cycle (no rational 6-cycle);
      it is the unique centred monic quadratic over Q with a nondegenerate AP-supported 3-cycle; determinant-one
      lift B with B^3=-I.  THM-4146-*: trace-one SL_2 lift, integral hexagon on X^2+2XY+13Y^2=48, the signed
      Pythagorean template forces the 3:4:5 class and 29=5^2+2^2.  Rational 3-cycles of x^2+c: Poonen 1998 (CITED).
(ii) 'the inverse square horizon (Z,Z^2) cancels the spatial translation after three steps': SCOPE, no map found;
      the dynamics is x -> x^2 - 29/16, a single quadratic map, and its period-3 orbit is the content of THM-4139.

