(i) REFUTED ('endpoints 1, 26, 80'): the peaks of 5,7,23 are 8,26,80 (shortcut) or 16,52,160 (full map);
      1 is the sink of every orbit, not a peak.  Incidentally 8=3^2-1, 26=5^2+1, 80=9^2-1 with bases 3,5,9.
(ii) PROVED: for an odd seed n>1 the shortcut peak p is even (an odd p>1 is followed by (3p+1)/2>p), p=(3m+1)/2
      with m odd and 3m+1 = 0 mod 4, so m = 1 mod 4 and p = 2 mod 6.  Under the full map the peak is 3m+1 = 4 mod 6.
      FINITE-EXACT: all 49,999 shortcut peaks (odd seeds 3..10^5) are 2 mod 6; all full-map peaks are 4 mod 6.
      max peak/seed among them: 10112.041 at seed 77671 (peak 785412368)
      PROVED (hostile to 'growth bound by area'): C^j(2^k-1) = 3^j 2^{k-j} - 1 for j<=k, so the seed 2^k-1
      climbs to 3^k-1 ~ n^{log2 3}; peak/seed is unbounded (checked k=5,10,20).
