   1048575  20  [1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, ...]   24  36561584390144 36561584390144 -3638566269747200        False
    PROVED (inherited, 05-knowledge/results/collatz_blueprint_20260921_synthesis.md section 6): with K_j the partial
      sums of the halving word and B = sum_j 3^{L-1-j} 2^{K_j}, 2^K T^L(n) = 3^L n + B, hence
      T^L(n) < n  iff  3^L n + B < 2^K n.  The paste's inequality is exactly this certificate.
    The paste supplies no argument that every fixed n>1 eventually acquires a word with positive margin; 'peaks
      run out of volume' is not a statement about any n.  The obligation remains OPEN, verbatim as in the audit.
    27 reaches 1 after L=41 odd steps (K=70, total 111 full-map steps).
      FINITE-EXACT: for n=27 the first L with positive margin is L=37 (K=59, T^37(27)=23; 37+59=96 is the
        classical total stopping time of 27 under the full map).

